---
/** EMAIL HEADER READER Model 1, interactive instrument for the reading-email-headers
 *  tutorial. Renders the sample (or pasted) header as a line-by-line view,
 * shows the three authentication verdicts, and explains each one
 * directly under its row. Opening a row highlights the matching
 * line(s) in the header so the reader learns what to look for.
 *
 * Progressive: without JS the static SVG fallback stays visible; with JS the
 * instrument comes alive and the fallback is hidden.
 */
---

<div class="email-fallback" id="emailFallback">
  <img
    src="/tutorials/reading-email-headers/demo.svg"
    alt="Terminal recording: reading a spoofed email's SPF/DKIM/DMARC verdicts and confirming the sending domain has no authentication posture."
    loading="lazy"
    decoding="async"
  />
  <p class="lab-instrument-caption">
    Reading the three authentication verdicts off one header, then confirming what the sending domain actually publishes with dig.
  </p>
  <p class="email-fallback-note">
    This is the static version. The interactive reader on this page needs JavaScript.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="email-reader" id="emailReaderRoot">
  <div class="email-reader-stage">
    <div class="email-reader-brand">
      <span class="email-reader-name">EMAIL HEADER READER</span>
      <span class="email-reader-model">Model 1 &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; tap a row to see what to look for</span>
    </div>

    <p class="email-reader-intro">
      A worked sample is loaded below. Tap a verdict row to highlight the line it
      comes from and read what it means. Clear it to paste your own.
    </p>

    <div class="email-header-view" id="emailHeaderView">
      <pre class="email-header-pre" id="emailHeaderPre"></pre>
    </div>

    <textarea
      id="emailHeaderInput"
      class="email-input is-paste"
      spellcheck="false"
      autocomplete="off"
      autocapitalize="off"
      aria-label="Paste a raw email header"
    >Return-Path: &lt;alerts@dalimnthefoob.co&gt;
Received: from 89.144.44.17 (mscode.pl [89.144.44.17]) by mx.outlook.com with Microsoft SMTP Server; Mon, 28 Jul 2026 09:14:02 +0000
Received: from mx.outlook.com (mail.protection.outlook.com) by outlook.office365.com with HTTPS; Mon, 28 Jul 2026 09:14:03 +0000
Received: from outlook.office365.com by prod.outlook.com node1; Mon, 28 Jul 2026 09:14:04 +0000
Received: from prod.outlook.com node1 by prod.outlook.com node2; Mon, 28 Jul 2026 09:14:05 +0000
Authentication-Results: mx.outlook.com;
    dkim=fail (no signature for key);
    spf=fail (smtp.mailfrom=dalimnthefoob.co);
    dmarc=fail (p=none - no policy published)
Received-SPF: fail (dalimnthefoob.co: domain not designated as permitted sender)
From: "Account Security" &lt;alerts@dalimnthefoob.co&gt;
Subject: Someone tried to log in To Your Account
To: undisclosed-recipients:;
Date: Mon, 28 Jul 2026 09:14:02 +0000
Message-ID: &lt;phish-2026-07-28@dalimnthefoob.co&gt;</textarea>

    <div class="email-reader-controls">
      <button type="button" class="email-toggle-btn" id="emailPasteToggle">Paste your own</button>
      <button type="button" class="email-read-btn" id="emailReadBtn">Read it</button>
    </div>

    <dl class="email-verdicts">
      <details class="email-verdict-row" id="emailSpfRow">
        <summary class="email-verdict-summary">
          <span class="email-verdict-label">SPF</span>
          <span class="email-verdict-val email-verdict--unknown" id="emailSpfVal">-</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="email-verdict-explain">
          <p><strong>What to look for:</strong> the line starting with <code>Authentication-Results</code> (or <code>Received-SPF</code>).</p>
          <p><strong>What it means:</strong> SPF tells you whether the email came from a server the domain allows to send for it. <code>pass</code> means the server was on the domain's allowed list; <code>fail</code> means it was not; <code>none</code> means the domain published no allowed list at all.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="email-verdict-row" id="emailDkimRow">
        <summary class="email-verdict-summary">
          <span class="email-verdict-label">DKIM</span>
          <span class="email-verdict-val email-verdict--unknown" id="emailDkimVal">-</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="email-verdict-explain">
          <p><strong>What to look for:</strong> the <code>Authentication-Results</code> line (the <code>dkim=</code> part), or a <code>DKIM-Signature</code> line.</p>
          <p><strong>What it means:</strong> DKIM is a signature on the message checked against the domain's key. <code>pass</code> means the signature matched; <code>fail</code> means it did not, or there was none; <code>none</code> means no signature was on the message to check.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <details class="email-verdict-row" id="emailDmarcRow">
        <summary class="email-verdict-summary">
          <span class="email-verdict-label">DMARC</span>
          <span class="email-verdict-val email-verdict--unknown" id="emailDmarcVal">-</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="email-verdict-explain">
          <p><strong>What to look for:</strong> the <code>Authentication-Results</code> line (the <code>dmarc=</code> part).</p>
          <p><strong>What it means:</strong> DMARC is the domain's rule for what receivers should do with mail that fails the other two. <code>pass</code> means the message followed the rule; <code>fail</code> means it broke a published rule; <code>none</code> means the domain published no rule at all. "no DMARC" is different from "DMARC fail."</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </dl>

    <p class="email-domain">
      Sending domain: <span id="emailDomain">-</span>
    </p>

    <p class="email-action" id="emailAction">Tap Read it to read the loaded sample, or clear it and paste your own.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .email-fallback.is-hidden { display: none; }
  .email-fallback-note {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, "Space Mono", ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted, #8a8478);
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .email-reader {
    display: none;
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule, #d8d2c4);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule, #d8d2c4);
  }
  .email-reader.is-live { display: block; }

  .email-reader-stage {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .email-reader-brand {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }
  .email-reader-name {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, "Space Mono", ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted, #8a8478);
  }
  .email-reader-model {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, "Space Mono", ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--ink-muted, #8a8478);
  }

  .email-reader-intro {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--ink, #2b2a26);
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .email-header-view.is-paste { display: none; }
  .email-input.is-paste { display: none; }

  .email-header-pre {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 9rem;
    max-height: 16rem;
    overflow: auto;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, "Space Mono", ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink, #2b2a26);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink, #1c1a16) 4%, transparent);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule, #d8d2c4);
    border-radius: 4px;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
  .email-header-line { display: block; padding: 0.05rem 0.15rem; border-radius: 2px; }
  .email-header-line.is-hit {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sage, #64705b) 28%, transparent);
    box-shadow: inset 2px 0 0 0 var(--sage, #64705b);
  }

  .email-input {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 9rem;
    resize: vertical;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, "Space Mono", ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    padding: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink, #2b2a26);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink, #1c1a16) 4%, transparent);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule, #d8d2c4);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .email-input:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--sage, #64705b); outline-offset: 1px; }

  .email-reader-controls { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .email-toggle-btn, .email-read-btn {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, "Space Mono", ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.45rem 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink, #2b2a26);
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--sage, #64705b);
    border-radius: 3px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .email-toggle-btn:hover, .email-read-btn:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sage, #64705b) 12%, transparent);
  }

  .email-verdicts { width: 100%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; margin: 0.25rem 0 0; }
  .email-verdict-row {
    width: 100%;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule, #d8d2c4);
  }
  .email-verdict-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .email-verdict-summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.25rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .email-verdict-summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .email-verdict-row[open] .email-verdict-summary {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sage, #64705b) 8%, transparent);
  }
  .email-verdict-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, "Space Mono", ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--ink, #2b2a26);
  }
  .email-verdict-val {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, "Space Mono", ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .email-verdict--pass { color: #4f9a5a; }
  .email-verdict--fail { color: #c25a4a; }
  .email-verdict--none { color: #b08a3a; }
  .email-verdict--unknown { color: var(--ink-muted, #8a8478); }
  .email-verdict-explain {
    padding: 0.5rem 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink, #2b2a26);
  }
  .email-verdict-explain p { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .email-verdict-explain p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .email-domain {
    width: 100%;
    font-family: var(--font-mono, "Space Mono", ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted, #8a8478);
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .email-domain #emailDomain { color: var(--ink, #2b2a26); }

  .email-action {
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--ink, #2b2a26);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule, #d8d2c4);
    padding: 0.75rem 0.25rem 0;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .email-reader { display: block; }
    .email-fallback { display: none; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { initEmailHeaderReader } from '../scripts/email-header-reader';
  initEmailHeaderReader();
</script>
